<title>BELGIUM: Lauda downplays high speed train threat.</title>
<headline>Lauda downplays high speed train threat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former Formula One racing champion and president of Austrian airline Lauda Air AG, Niki Lauda, on Wednesday played down the threat to European air transport from the high-speed train network.</p>
<p>&quot;The railway system in many European countries is in such a precarious state that it will take centuries before the system will function,&quot; he told Belgian Knack magazine in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;The (high-speed network) could become a competitor but not quite yet,&quot; he said.</p>
